m().\0A *\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_SUCCESS \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INVALID_SIGNATURE\0A *         The output was read successfully, but if differs from the expected\0A *         output.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INVALID_HANDLE\0A *         The key passed as the expected value does not exist.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INVALID_ARGUMENT\0A *         The key passed as the expected value has an invalid type.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_NOT_PERMITTED\0A *         The key passed as the expected value does not allow this usage or\0A *         this algorithm; or one of the inputs was a key whose policy didn't\0A *         allow #PSA_KEY_USAGE_VERIFY_DERIVATION.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_DATA\0A *                          The operation's capacity was less than\0A *                          the length of the expected value. In this case,\0A *                          the operation's capacity is set to 0, thus\0A *                          subsequent calls to this function will not\0A *                          succeed, even with a smaller expected output.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_MEMORY \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_COMMUNICATION_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_HARDWARE_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_CORRUPTION_DETECTED \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_STORAGE_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_BAD_STATE\0A *         The operation state is not valid (it must be active and completed\0A *         all required input steps), or the library has not been previously\0A *         initialized by psa_crypto_init().\0A *         It is implementation-dependent whether a failure to initialize\0A *         results in this error code.\0A */\0Apsa_status_t psa_key_derivation_verify_key(\0A    psa_key_derivation_operation_t *operation,\0A    psa_key_id_t expected);\0A\0A/** Abort a key derivation operation.\0A *\0A * Aborting an operation frees all associated r